# The worker images are built with the repository root as their context, but
# each Dockerfile copies exactly two things: entitybase-backend/ and its own
# worker directory. Everything else here was still being sent.
#
# The worst of it was entitybase-backend/.venv at 353MB, which is inside the
# path every worker copies - so it was both transferred and baked into the
# image, on every build, whether or not anything had changed.

# Virtualenvs, everywhere. The workers install their own with uv sync.
**/.venv
.venv

# Python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Frontend dependencies and build output
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Scratch clones: external/ is gitignored and hundreds of megabytes
external/

# Generated documentation and reports
site/
**/site/
.docs-site/
**/coverage/
coverage.txt
coverage.xml
coverage_below_threshold.txt
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Logs and local run output
*.log
**/var/